  "worked_solution": "Since we want to find the projection onto the $yz$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $x.$ First, we solve for $x$ in the equation of the plane, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+z & =4\\,\u27f9\\,x=4-z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $x$ into the equation of the sphere, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4-z)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =18 \\\\ (16-8z+{z}^{2})+(y-1)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =18 \\\\ (y-1)^{2}+2{z}^{2}-8z+16 & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by completing the square for the variable $z$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-1)^{2}+2{z}^{2}-8z+16 & =18 \\\\ (y-1)^{2}+2{z}^{2}-8z+8 & =10 \\\\ (y-1)^{2}+2({z}^{2}-4z+4) & =10 \\\\ (y-1)^{2}+2(z-2)^{2} & =10 \\\\ \\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{10}+\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{5} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the projection of the intersection is the ellipse $\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{10}+\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{5}=1.$",
